==Polish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈvwɔxɨ/|lang=pl}}
* {{audio|Pl-Włochy.ogg|audio|lang=pl}}

===Etymology===
Most likely from {{etyl|la|pl}} {{m|la|Volsci}}, an Italic tribe, rather than from {{etyl|gem-pro|-}} {{m|gem-pro|*walhaz}} from {{m|la|Volcae}} (see [[w:Volcae|Volcae]]), origin of terms for [[Wales]], [[Vlach]], [[Wallachia]], ''[[et cetera]]''. Historically the tribe's name has been linked to an animal, likely {{etyl|cel-gau|pl}} {{m|cel-gau|*wolko-||wolf}}, as Caesar described the Celts having fought with huge dogs, in turn from {{etyl|ine-pro|pl}} {{m|ine-pro|*wĺ̥kʷos}}.<ref>Caesar, Commentarii de Bello Gallico</ref>

